  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is running 7% under trailing-30d productivity per groomer ($432 vs $469/groomer-day), and that's the real story below yesterday's flat headline. Core grooms actually lifted 7% week-over-week, which is solid, but add-on attach collapsed to 67% from 95%\u2014your team didn't upsell yesterday. MTD you're down 12% in absolute dollars, but DOW-adjusted you're only 10% short of expectation, meaning calendar mix accounts for about 2 points; the rest is real. Appointments are down 10% MTD, which signals visit-cadence drift\u2014your lapse pool of 516 customers represents $318k in annual value and needs activation. The bright spot: year-to-date you're up 37% in revenue and 36% in appointments versus last year, which is genuinely exceptional growth.\n\nHicksville is the inverse problem. Yesterday's $182/groomer-day is a 55% miss versus your trailing-30d baseline of $408, but you only had two groomers on the floor\u2014this was a capacity call, not performance. MTD you're actually up 6% and tracking 2% ahead of DOW-adjusted expectation, so the operation is healthy. The concern: zero bather hours yesterday and zero scheduled today and tomorrow. Bathers drive grooming velocity; you've got a 22-groomer-day week ahead but no bathing support to feed them.\n\nGlen Cove is parked: zero grooming activity, zero bathers scheduled next 7 days, and it's functioning as retail-only on skeleton crew. That's a strategic choice, not an operational miss, but it's not producing.\n\nPort Washington today: 6 groomers, 0 bathers; tomorrow 7 groomers, 15 bathers; next 7 days 36 groomer-days, 83 bathers. Hicksville today: 3 groomers, 0 bathers; tomorrow 4 groomers, 0 bathers; next 7 days 22 groomer-days, 0 bathers."
